"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-003","sourceId":"b3-012-003","sourceIndex":2,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,17],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"We sometimes imagine a desert island to be a sort of paradise where the sun always shines.","start":26.36,"end":32.34,"score":0.975,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-004","sourceId":"b3-012-004","sourceIndex":3,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,6],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Life there is simple and good.","start":33.66,"end":35.76,"score":0.993,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-005","sourceId":"b3-012-005","sourceIndex":4,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,12],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Ripe fruit falls from the trees and you never have to work.","start":36.55,"end":40.07,"score":0.954,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-006","sourceId":"b3-012-006","sourceIndex":5,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,10],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"The other side of the picture is quite the opposite.","start":40.79,"end":43.26,"score":0.962,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-007","sourceId":"b3-012-007","sourceIndex":6,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,7],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Life on a desert island is wretched.","start":44.25,"end":46.88,"score":0.958,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-008","sourceId":"b3-012-008","sourceIndex":7,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,17],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"You either starve to death or live like Robinson Crusoe, waiting for a boat which never comes.","start":47.54,"end":53.96,"score":0.944,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-009","sourceId":"b3-012-009","sourceIndex":8,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,22],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Perhaps there is an element of truth in both these pictures, but few of us have had the opportunity to find out.","start":55.3,"end":62.2,"score":0.952,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-010","sourceId":"b3-012-010","sourceIndex":9,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,17],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Two men who recently spent five days on a coral island wished they had stayed there longer.","start":63.66,"end":69.18,"score":0.968,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-011","sourceId":"b3-012-011","sourceIndex":10,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,17],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"They were taking a badly damaged boat from the Virgin Islands to Miami to have it repaired.","start":70.24,"end":76.18,"score":0.966,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-012","sourceId":"b3-012-012","sourceIndex":11,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,8],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"During the journey, their boat began to sink.","start":76.84,"end":79.6,"score":0.985,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-013-p01","sourceId":"b3-012-013","sourceIndex":12,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,9],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"They quickly loaded a small rubber dinghy with food,","start":80.26,"end":83.08,"score":0.926,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-013-p02","sourceId":"b3-012-013","sourceIndex":12,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[9,31],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"matches, and cans of beer and rowed for a few miles across the Caribbean until they arrived at a tiny coral island.","start":83.44,"end":91.13,"score":0.937,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-014","sourceId":"b3-012-014","sourceIndex":13,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,22],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"There were hardly any trees on the island and there was no water, but this did not prove to be a problem.","start":92.58,"end":98.8,"score":0.994,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-015","sourceId":"b3-012-015","sourceIndex":14,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,8],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"The men collected rainwater in the rubber dinghy.","start":99.8,"end":102.71,"score":0.854,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-016","sourceId":"b3-012-016","sourceIndex":15,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,14],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"As they had brought a spear gun with them, they had plenty to eat.","start":103.6,"end":107.143,"score":0.961,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-017","sourceId":"b3-012-017","sourceIndex":16,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,17],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"They caught lobster and fish every day, and as one of them put it 'ate like kings'.","start":107.68,"end":113.39,"score":0.912,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-012-018","sourceId":"b3-012-018","sourceIndex":17,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,19],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"When a passing tanker rescued them five days later, both men were genuinely sorry that they had to leave.","start":114.2,"end":121.6,"score":0.971,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]}]}
